Well, I finally got NetHack to run under Windows.  I would like to offer my
thanks to Todd Moore and Josh Hall for their help.  Here's what I had to do to
get it to work:

Having only 4Meg ram on my computer, I had to make a permanent 6Meg swap file
for virtual memory under "386 Enhanced" in the Control Panel.  I also had to
create a NH.PIF file from the Pif Editor default with the following changes:

Video Memory:  * High Graphics
Memory Requirements:    required:  640  desired:  -1

This setup works for nh313386.exe and chrhac23.

